**How to implement.** The reference kit is committed as AT-2's build writes it, once, and never by hand (001 §Q 'Section 12 creates them by running the build below once, through the app's own folder `KitProxy`, and commits the result. They are never hand-written'; 001 §S12 'create the committed kits … `data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy/` (with AT-2's five generated observation files)'; 001 §1). (1) Shared with AT-1: the file-by-file comparison step 428's fact makes inline (the two folders' relative paths, `.oc/` left out of both, then each file's bytes, a difference naming the built folder's absolute path, the first differing relative path and why: missing, extra or different bytes) becomes the private `assertSameKitFiles (built : KitFolder) (other : KitFolder) : unit`, documented in one line citing spec 0050 S12.2, which step 428's and step 430's facts call, their assertions kept. (2) The fact `the built absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit equals the committed kit file by file` in `KitAcceptanceTests`: over `absorbingBuild` (step 432), `CommittedKit.AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyKit.tryFindFolder` (step 431) answers the committed folder, `None` failing the fact naming the built folder; then `assertSameKitFiles` of the built folder and it: every kit file at the root, every file under `library/` and every file under `data/`, the five observation files included, so the committed observations are what the seeds regenerate (001 §Q AT-2). It reads the committed kit and writes nothing there (.spec-md §4 'Tests' data'). (3) The committed kit, created by this step once: run the fact (`kit-acceptance`, filtered to it); it fails, because `data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy/` does not exist, and names its built folder; copy every file of that folder except those under `.oc/` into `data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy/`, keeping their relative paths and bytes; run the fact again, and it passes. The files are the kit file, the eight `<label>.item-json`, the five `<plate>.setup-json`, the five `<plate>.experiment-json`, `AbsorbingTriclinic.study-json`, `AbsorbingTriclinic@20260601T120100Z.fitrun-json`, the five `data/noisy-observations-seed-<n>.csv`, and `library/`'s four snapshots, each `library/<id>@v1.<kind>-json`: the material `81e1d115-5d06-4337-80fd-50765a403de7`, the sample `af711361-2854-4b61-ade4-bdb47a184d9f`, and the `heNe633` preset and the Mueller polarimeter model under the GUIDs the built-in catalogue froze (steps 20, 209). All are LF text, which `.gitattributes`' `* text=auto eol=lf` keeps byte-identical; `git check-ignore` matches none of them, and `/data/*/.oc/` stays ignored (.spec-md §10.6). (4) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha step 428 adds ('The reference kits are AT-1's and AT-2's output, never hand-edited'): its sentence on the optics-mueller kit gains, in no more than one line, that `data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy/` is exactly what the AT-2 build writes, its five observation files included, and that a change to what the build writes re-runs `the built absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit equals the committed kit file by file` and re-commits the files it names in the same step. The bullet stays within four lines, and nothing else in the file changes.

**Acceptance.** After the kit is committed, `data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy/` MUST hold exactly the kit files, library snapshots and five observation files AT-2's build writes, `the built absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit equals the committed kit file by file` MUST pass, and AGENTS.md's reference-kit gotcha MUST name the AT-2 kit; AT-1's equality and Send facts MUST compare through `assertSameKitFiles`; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `the built absorbing-biaxial-noisy kit equals the committed kit file by file`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s42 invariants MUST pass.
